      "text": [
        " أَتَى رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) رَجُلٌ فَقَالَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَوْصِنِي فَكَانَ فِيمَا أَوْصَاهُ أَنْ قَالَ الْقَ أَخَاكَ بِوَجْهٍ مُنْبَسِطٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Mahboubn, from Hisham Bin Salim, from Abu Baseer, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup style=\"font-weight: normal\">asws</sup> having said: ‘A man came over to Rasool-Allah<sup style=\"font-weight: normal\">saww</sup>, so he said, ‘O Rasool-Allah<sup style=\"font-weight: normal\">saww</sup>! Advise me’. So, among what he<sup style=\"font-weight: normal\">saww</sup> advised him was that he<sup style=\"font-weight: normal\">saww</sup> said: ‘Meet your brother with a cheerful face’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn Mahbub from Hisham ibn Salim from abu Basir from abu Ja’far (a.s.) who has said the following: “Once a man came to the Messenger of Allah, saying, ‘O Messenger of Allah, confer upon me good advice.’ Of the advice given to him was this: ‘Meet your brethren (fellow human beings) with open and delightful face.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
